#Problem APEX 1.6.28
## DBsubject(Calculus - single variable)
## DBchapter(Limits and continuity)
## DBsection(Limits at infinity, horizontal and oblique asymptotes)
## KEYWORDS('asymptote','horizontal')
## Institution(Valdosta State University)
## Author(S. V. Ault)
## Level(2)
## TitleText1('APEX Calculus')
## AuthorText1('Hartman')
## EditionText1('3.0')
## Section1('1.6')
## Problem1('28')

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');
Context("Numeric");

$a = random(-9,  9);
$b = random(-9,  9);
$c = random(-9,  9);
$d = random( 1,  9);
$e = random(-9, -1);

$f   = Formula("(x^3+$a x^2+$b x+$c)/($d+$e x^2)")->reduce;
$ans = Compute("inf");

BEGIN_PGML
Evaluate the limit.

[``  \lim_{x \to -\infty} [$f] = ``] [_]{$ans}{8}

See [@helpLink("limit")@]*.
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
Note that the numerator has a higher degree than the denominator.
For very *negative* values of [`x`],
[```
  [$f] \approx
  \frac{x^3}{[$e] x^2} = \frac{x}{[$e]} \to \infty.
```]
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
